# Immediately stop message processing, discard every trajectory point the
# controller has already accepted, and exit the active motion mode.
#
# Unlike 'stop_traj_mode' -- which refuses while the increment queue still holds
# work -- this service always exits the motion mode, whatever the queue holds.
# Discarding accepted motion is the intended behaviour, not a side effect: this
# is the escalation path for when a graceful stop cannot be honoured.
#
# >>> SOFTWARE STOP ONLY - NOT A SAFETY-RATED EMERGENCY STOP <<<
# This stops the arm as fast as software can, and no faster. It is subject to
# controller scheduling, message-processing latency and the servo deceleration
# ramp, and it does nothing at all if MotoROS2 or the Agent link is unhealthy.
# Only the physical safety circuit (E-stop button, safety fence, PFL) provides
# emergency-stop assurance. Do NOT present this service to an operator as an
# emergency stop.
#
# NOTE: as with 'stop_traj_mode', the underlying stop sequence toggles the
# controller's HOLD state ON and then OFF. If an operator had set HOLD at the
# pendant, that HOLD is RELEASED by this service.
#
# The request is empty: the abort is unconditional and takes no arguments.

---
# TRUE if the abort completed: message processing stopped, every accepted point
# discarded, and the motion mode exited.
#
# FALSE means the stop could not be confirmed - message processing did not
# quiesce in time, or an increment queue was locked and could not be cleared.
# The motion mode is exited either way, but motion may not have stopped: treat
# the controller as unsafe and use the physical E-stop.
bool success

# Human-readable detail, always populated. On failure it names what could not be
# confirmed.
string message
